    "updated_at": "2019-08-19T19:58:45Z",
    "body": "I don't understand what this statement means. Web IDL interface definitions are essentially ways of generating code for JavaScript classes. Attributes generate getters/setters (accessor properties) on the class's prototype. Operations generate methods (function-valued data properties) on the class's prototype. Etc.\r\n\r\n\"Objects implementing an interface\" are objects which are instances of those generated classes. As such, under a normal environment (where the page developer hasn't messed with any prototype chains), there will appear to be accessible properties corresponding to each of the class's prototype properties, via JavaScript's prototypal inheritance system.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
